  "pressure_sample_boundary": "Before SIGTERM:80 actual failed Prepare calls plus startup event; enqueued66, written1, queued64, dropped15. One failed record in flight. Later shutdown drops are not asserted equal to this earlier sample. Queue acceptance and visible header are not audit durability ACKs.",
  "cold_visibility_boundary": "Record-data never writes header5, so cold committed prefix4. Header-publish has completed checked data Sync, but selected header Sync is unACKed: cold may validly observe4 or5. Actual current experiment observed5. Ordinary unfiltered validated writer continues without reset/repair.",
  "fault_boundary": "Only source-bound ordinary root TGID/start/ELF inode/control; fixed FSYNC+EXIT_GROUP inherited test observer. Target ring FSYNC receives no response, only actual EXIT_GROUP1 is continued. Known process really reaped, both IDs ENOENT with listener still open. Not a filesystem D, media fault or security-policy implementation.",
  "lifecycle_boundary": "Two real guests: raw accepted writer progresses and session route stays intact while ring FSYNC is held and queue full. Ordinary Delete/revoke stops execution and separately durable private GC/quota0 before log resolution. Inputs change only owned L1 kernel/initrd/workspace modes, restore original0444/unchanged bytes; no authority patch. Cleanup/receipt may sync filesystem, not an unsynced-media cut.",
